+
+# Booking cancellation and refund rules
+
+## Context
+Customers ask to cancel bookings. The request defines `cancel(bookingId, at)` returning
+`{ bookingId, refund }`, a cancelled booking freeing its equipment, and a single cancellation per
+booking. It does not say how the refund is computed, and no earlier decision covers it.
+
+## Decision (proposed, awaiting approval of the refund scale)
+- `at` is an ISO-8601 UTC string; an invalid one, or an unknown booking id, throws.
+- Cancelling twice throws; the booking is then no longer held, so its period is free again for
+  `book` and `availability` (half-open overlap rule unchanged).
+- Refund, in integer cents of the booking `total`, by notice = booking `start` - `at`:
+  - 48 hours or more: 100% of the total;
+  - from 24 hours up to (excluding) 48 hours: 50%, rounded down to the cent;
+  - under 24 hours, including after the start: nothing (0).
+- Cancelling after the booking `end` throws (nothing left to cancel).
+
+## Consequences
+The 48h / 24h thresholds and the 100% / 50% / 0% percentages are an assumption to be confirmed.
+Changing them later only touches one refund function.
